            },
            {
                "id": 38277668800,
                "preferredName": "Rafael A. Rodríguez-Solís",
                "firstName": "Rafael A.",
                "lastName": "Rodríguez-Solís"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "A new design of a compact radiometer intended for uav application is presented. radiometers in spaceborne systems tend to be affected by clouds and atmospheric noise. the design of this airborne sensor is explained and it is divided into three phases: 1) a new dual-band antenna array and l-band receiver; 2) the design of the ka-band receiver and testing of the array; 3) the implementation and testing of the low frequency system on a controlled field. the microstrip patch array and slot array designs are presented. the l-band array gain is 14.337 db, and the beamwidth is 30 degrees, and the ka-band array gain is 12.47 db. the designs of the l-band and ka-band receiver are explained, and results of the first prototype of the l-band receiver are similar to results obtained by spaceborne sensors.",
